# Data integrity

Cloud orgs, sites, gateways, generators, and telemetry are durable Convex records.

## Never

- Add destructive DB resets to ordinary deploys/init.
- Auto-delete orgs/devices on startup.
- Replace real cloud data with demo seed in non-demo flows.
- Convert missing telemetry into `0`.
- Silently discard valid telemetry.
- Treat Modbus/Wi-Fi Soft-AP settings as cloud-persisted unless proven.

## Empty UI investigation order

1. Frontend Convex URL · 2. Deployment identity · 3. Auth/session · 4. Org membership/permissions · 5. Query loading/errors · 6. Whether records exist · 7. Persistence last

Do not conclude data was deleted because a page looks empty.

## Telemetry

- Preserve valid negatives and power-factor signs.
- Distinguish source timestamps vs gateway receipt time; never treat uptime as wall clock.
- Distinguish stale vs true zero. Handle duplicates/out-of-order deliberately.
- Preserve raw Modbus evidence when available.
